  <compounddef id="Manual-example" kind="example">
    <compoundname>Manual</compoundname>
    <briefdescription>
<para>construction (not typical) </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>construction (not typical) <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">PoolAllocator*<sp/>raw_pool<sp/>=<sp/>//<sp/>...<sp/>created<sp/>via<sp/>factory<sp/>...;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">cslt::UniquePtr&lt;PoolAllocator,<sp/>PoolDeleter&gt;<sp/>pool(raw_pool,<sp/>PoolDeleter{});</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">//<sp/>Automatic<sp/>cleanup<sp/>when<sp/>pool<sp/>goes<sp/>out<sp/>of<sp/>scope</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para><simplesect kind="warning"><para>Never call ::operator delete directly on a PoolAllocator created by a factory method. Always use PoolDeleter or let UniquePtr handle it.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="warning"><para>For Stack pools, ensure the buffer outlives the pool. The deleter doesn&apos;t free the buffer (user owns it), but the pool must be destroyed before the buffer goes out of scope.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para>PoolAllocator::Heap() Creates pool with owned arena </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para>PoolAllocator::WithArena() Creates pool with borrowed arena </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para>PoolAllocator::Stack() Creates pool with owned arena in user buffer </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para>ArenaDeleter For arena cleanup details <programlisting filename="Manual"></programlisting> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
